  "hypothesis": "The hardcoded JS clear-level temperature overwrites the branch default after public reset_level coder initialization.",
  "expectedBehavior": "Reset restores hot1 on hellish branches and temperate0 elsewhere, independent of prior authored temperature flags.",
  "observedBehavior": "Nine Gehennom targets: C1 versus JS0. Nine Dungeons of Doom controls: C0 and JS0. Three valid floors per branch times three prior temperature values.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "compiled_oracle",
    "scope": "Production JS reset API on empty construction levels; exact C reset/clear/In_hell routines with typed non-temperature adapters. Temperature output only.",
    "limitations": [
      "Nine targets: actual generated Gehennom dungeon record, valid floors1..3, prior cold/temperate/hot flags. Nine controls use actual Dungeons of Doom floors1..3 and the same prior flags. One reset-temperature cause, not nine independent bugs.",
      "JS uses newgame_pre_mklev with fixed seed/date/options, supported mklev specialLevelLoader and public des.level_flags/des.reset_level. The empty loader snapshot has no monsters or stairs. LoaderDone intentionally stops after reset observation before finalization; this is not a full shipped game recording or score claim.",
      "C executes exact registered lspo_reset_level, full clear_level_structures and In_hell. Typed structs supply accessed fields and actual dungeon hellish input. C cleanup/rectangle/coordinate hooks and pre-reset preparation are interfaces for absent resources, and coder creation is a valid allocation adapter. They do not model full reset behavior. The final tested temperature assignment in clear_level_structures overwrites all earlier temperature state; this dominance is why their internals are unnecessary for this flag witness.",
      "No C Lua VM is added: lspo_reset_level ignores Lua arguments beyond nonnull state. The typed Lua token supplies that valid nonnull branch. Full C flags/terrain/resources are not compared; placeholder rm/glyph fields support the exact clear body only. No save-state export or blocked prerequisites are used.",
      "Normal loader order runs clear then coder initialization, restoring hot1; reset order initializes coder then clears, exposing temperate0. Shipped callers of reset_level and downstream temperature-sensitive behavior remain unestablished. No general initialization/finalization/runtime equivalence claim.",
      "Target runner records but does not enforce original JS hashes, allowing the same command to pass after Main repairs the cause. C source identities and exact copied functions are enforced. Deliberate failing target is ordinary .mjs and is not in default CI.",
      "Cave-cap, bottom-level stair search and three parked gaps remain unresolved. Existing Main-owned repairs and all denied investigations remain separate."
    ]
  },
